# Selector (Polymorphic Schema Input)

<h2 id="purpose">Purpose</h2>

A selector tells Home Assistant what kind of value a form field needs, and Home Assistant draws the matching input. A `number` selector draws a number box or a slider, a `boolean` selector a switch, an `area` selector an area picker. Selectors are used in the automation and script editors, in blueprints, in the forms that run actions and in integration settings.

They appear in Home Assistant’s own screens and dialogs, not as dashboard cards. This page is for people who write selectors or review forms built from them. For forms as a whole, see [Form & Schema Form](form-and-schema-form.html) and [Schema selectors and configuration forms](../home-assistant/schema-selectors.html).

